# Normalize source files to LF in the repo and on checkout, so the same
# input produces the same bytes on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...but never touch the build. dist/index.html is a single self-contained
# file whose Content-Security-Policy pins a SHA-256 hash of its own inline
# <script>. Any line-ending conversion rewrites those bytes, the hash stops
# matching, and the browser silently refuses to run the script - the page
# loads blank and the tool is dead, with nothing in the UI to say why. On
# Windows, Git's default core.autocrlf=true does exactly that conversion on
# every clone and checkout.
#
# (A later, more specific pattern wins, so this overrides the rule above.)
*.html -text
